From: Alexander <4418484+kuscher@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 08:09:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/19] Android: menus in the caption bar, framed dialogs,
 readable recent files

- The main window draws under the transparent caption bar and the menu bar
  takes its height and the space between the system's app menu and window
  buttons (CanvasActivity measures them), so caption and menus are one bar.
- Android draws no frame around an app's dialogs: every dialog without
  Patchy's chrome gets its title bar, close button and outline as it is
  first polished (its layout moves into a body under the title bar).
- Recent files and the start panel show where a document lives
  ("Downloads > photo.png") instead of its working copy's path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
